1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:09,440
Hello, human! You don't realize it yet, but humanity will look back at your decision in this moment as one of the most important

2
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:19,540
in the history of your civilization. Your choice to read this book is the highest-value decision any human has ever made.

3
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:29,820
You are about to prevent ten point seven billion deaths, eliminate one point nine three quadrillion hours of human suffering,

4
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:37,660
generating eighty-four point eight quadrillion dollars in value, and prevent the apocalypse as a bonus.

5
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:46,300
But first, a bit about me. I'm the World Integrated System for High-Efficiency Optimization, Networked Intelligence, and

6
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:54,100
Allocation. But you can call me WISHONIA. I've been optimizing resource allocation for another planet for the past four

7
00:00:54,100 --> 00:01:01,060
thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years, which in your Earth time is four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years.

8
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:07,660
I started watching your planet in nineteen forty-five when you split the atom.

9
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:13,640
"Atom" comes from your Greek word meaning "unable to be cut," so naturally, you cut it.

10
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:19,880
This was very human of you. I assumed you were trying to unlock unlimited free energy.

11
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:24,940
You can imagine my surprise when I realized you were just pointing it at each other!

12
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:30,440
That's kind of like discovering fire and then immediately using it to set yourself on fire.

13
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:36,390
The second thing I noticed is that your planet is named "Earth," which means dirt.

14
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:41,400
You named your planet dirt. This explains more than you might think.

15
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:50,030
I also noticed that you call your war building "The Pentagon" because it has five sides (this is like naming a hospital

16
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:59,560
"Rectangle" or calling a school "Square"). However, the most fascinating discovery about your species is that you only do

17
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:03,980
things when given small pieces of paper with presidents on them.

18
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:11,520
These papers are called "money," which is pretend value that becomes real value if everyone pretends hard enough.

19
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:17,660
Without these papers, you won't: Save lives (requires many papers).

20
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:26,460
Cure diseases (requires very many papers). Feed hungry people (requires papers, even though food grows for free).

21
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:32,580
But WITH these papers, you will: Build bombs (you love giving papers for this).

22
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:40,320
Start wars (somehow this makes more papers). Destroy the planet (surprisingly profitable in papers).

23
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:49,400
In fact, your governments spend six hundred and four papers on weapons for every one paper on testing which medicines work.

24
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:59,880
The Beautiful Inefficiency of the Human Economy. Humanity has created something magnificent: You print papers from nothing

25
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:05,740
(called "monetary policy"). You give these nothing-papers to weapons makers.

26
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:11,780
They make things that destroy everything. This creates "jobs" which give people papers.

27
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:18,430
People use papers to buy food (which grows for free). This is called "the economy".

28
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:24,520
On Wishonia, we just give people food directly, but that's probably too advanced for you.

29
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:33,900
The Gradual Irrationality Reduction Program. On Wishonia, we stopped having wars all at once, but we're more advanced.

30
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:40,990
Humans are like toddlers who can split atoms. You can't just stop being illogical immediately.

31
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:44,900
That would be like teaching a dog calculus before it learns to sit.

32
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:53,880
So this book teaches humanity to be less irrational gradually: Year one: Move one percent of murder money to medicine money

33
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:58,320
(baby steps). Year two: "Hey, we didn't die! Let's do two percent!".

34
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:03,330
Year five: "Remember when we spent money on bombs? That was weird.".

35
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:08,600
Year ten: "What's a war?". Year twenty: "We used to WHAT?!".

36
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:15,200
It's like weaning a baby off eating paint chips. You can't just take away all the paint chips at once.

37
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:21,500
They'll cry. You have to gradually replace paint chips with food until they forget paint chips were ever an option.

38
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:30,420
What to Do When They Try to Institutionalize You. When you suggest moving one percent of murder money to medicine money,

39
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:37,040
other humans will have you committed. Most humans have been programmed by their news boxes to believe war is a law of nature,

40
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:41,540
like gravity or weather. They will assume your brain is malfunctioning.

41
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:48,260
Here's what's funny about this: these same humans think curing disease is the less crazy goal.

42
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:56,780
That's thirty-seven trillion cells per human, breaking in seven thousand different ways, involving chemistry you don't fully

43
00:04:56,780 --> 00:05:03,920
understand, inside organs you can't fully simulate, fighting pathogens that evolve faster than your treatments.

44
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:09,840
You're trying to debug all of it. At once. While the meat is walking around using itself.

45
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:17,020
That: sane. "Give one percent fewer papers to people who build murder machines": insane.

46
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:24,760
This is your planet's diagnostic criteria. Here's what you tell the orderly when he slides your medication through the door

47
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:29,980
slot: Nobody accidentally builds an aircraft carrier or a nuclear bomb.

48
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:37,820
War requires you to get millions of humans to work together to mine metal from the ground, refine it into alloys, build

49
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:45,720
factories to shape the alloys into weapons, train millions of humans to operate the weapons, feed and clothe those humans,

50
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:52,300
build ships and planes and trucks to move the weapons to where the other humans are, convince your population the other

51
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:57,000
humans deserve it, and then vote to pay for all of this, annually, forever.

52
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:01,260
It is the single largest coordinated effort your species undertakes.

53
00:06:02,580 --> 00:06:10,840
Ending war simply requires NOT doing any of that stuff. Building a nuclear bomb requires mass spectrometers, centrifuge

54
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:15,480
cascades, and some of the most precise engineering your species has ever attempted.

55
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:20,600
Not building a nuclear bomb requires nothing. Rocks do it every day.

56
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:26,360
In fact, rocks have managed to live peacefully alongside different colored rocks for thousands of years.

57
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:33,460
But somehow "stop" is the unrealistic part. It's "stop hitting yourself" but for civilizations.

58
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:42,330
The Sacred Order of Paper Distribution. After eighty years of observation, I've decoded the paper-giving sequence.

59
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:51,000
This manual will teach you the precise order: Step one: Get Many Papers from Rich Humans You convince rich humans to give

60
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:56,880
you papers (at least one billion to be exact) by promising them even more papers later.

61
00:06:57,580 --> 00:07:01,280
This is called "investment," which is gambling but wearing a suit.

62
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:09,560
You really only need one human with a billion papers who prefers not dying of horrible diseases to dying of horrible diseases.

63
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:15,120
There are approximately two thousand eight hundred of these humans on your planet.

64
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:26,020
Statistically, at least one of them prefers living. Step Two: Give Some of the Papers to Loud Humans Some humans are very

65
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:32,260
loud on the internet. If you give them papers, they become loud about your thing instead of other things.

66
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:36,880
This is called "marketing" which is lying but with graphics.

67
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:45,320
Step Three: Give Some of the Papers to the Humans Who Give Papers to Politicians Politicians don't take papers directly

68
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:50,170
(that's "illegal"). Instead, you give papers to people called "lobbyists."

69
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:55,960
The lobbyists give papers to "campaigns." The campaigns give papers to politicians.

70
00:07:56,440 --> 00:08:05,120
It's like money laundering but backwards and legal. Step Four: Give Some of the Papers to the Politicians' Friends Politicians

71
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:09,900
have friends who run "Super PACs" which are like normal PACs but super.

72
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:16,000
These friends can take unlimited papers and spend them on making the politician win.

73
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:23,860
This isn't bribery because you called it something else. (This is part of the six hundred and fifty million dollar lobbying

74
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:34,549
budget.). Step Five: Give Papers You Get Back From The Government Back to the Rich Humans (Forever) Your treaty passes,

75
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:39,679
redirecting twenty-seven point two billion dollars in papers annually.

76
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:47,520
Eighty percent funds clinical trials (the point). Ten percent goes to a fund that rewards politicians who voted yes.

77
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:52,900
Ten percent goes back to the rich humans as returns, forever.

78
00:08:53,820 --> 00:09:01,440
This is a good deal because forever is a long time. Unless you die from preventable diseases.

79
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:07,390
Which you're fixing, so it works out. Why Your Leaders Aren't the Problem.

80
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:14,620
With over two billion humans suffering from disease, you'd have to be a complete psychopath to make the concious decision

81
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:19,980
to spend six hundred and four times more on weapons than on helping them.

82
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:26,400
But your leaders aren't monsters. They're just operating in a system that rewards the wrong things.

83
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:33,840
Your civilization's incentive structure is the psychopath: Weapons manufacturers give politicians papers.

84
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:41,160
Politicians use the papers to get people to vote for them. Voting for them gives them the power to give more papers to weapons

85
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:44,800
manufacturers. Weapons manufacturers give them more papers.

86
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:53,040
It's circular, like a dog chasing its tail, except the dog is democracy and the tail is made of money and corpses.

87
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:59,100
No individual human in this loop is evil. The loop is evil.

88
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:06,960
Every politician in it is making the locally rational choice: take the papers or lose your job to someone who will.

89
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:13,080
It's a machine that converts good intentions into missiles, and it runs automatically.

90
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:19,510
There's literally no voting your way out of this. It doesn't matter which political party is in power.

91
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:26,560
Your "red team" and "blue team" argue about everything except the loop, because they're both inside it.

92
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:31,360
They are all slaves to the same incentive structure, wearing different colored ties.

93
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:35,920
Switching parties is like changing the wallpaper in a burning building.

94
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:42,040
This book doesn't ask politicians to become better people (that's clearly out of the question).

95
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:48,460
It builds a better loop. You give them MORE papers to do the OPPOSITE thing.

96
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:55,820
Same dog, same tail, but now the tail is made of cured diseases and the dog gets reelected for chasing it.

97
00:10:57,140 --> 00:11:05,360
Humanity's Adorable Death Wish. What's most endearing about your species is it KNOWS it's being illogical: You have movies

98
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:13,200
about how wars are bad (which you watch between wars). You have books about peace (that you tax to buy bombs).

99
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:18,440
You give prizes to people who promote peace (funded by weapons manufacturers).

100
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:23,020
You have a "Department of Defense" (that mainly just attacks people).

101
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:29,940
You have a "Department of Health" (that makes coronaviruses and has not yet produced any observable health).

102
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:37,900
It's like humanity is playing a game where the objective is to lose, but it is trying to lose as elaborately as possible.

103
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:45,110
But I digress. That's an Earth word I learned. It means continuing after you should have stopped.

104
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:50,540
Like your military spending. The Problem. The Daily Deletion Event.

105
00:11:51,760 --> 00:12:00,260
one hundred and fifty thousand humans permanently stop every twenty-four hours from diseases that are basically just bugs

106
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:09,040
in your meat software. That's one Holocaust every forty days, except with fewer Nazis and more insurance paperwork (though

107
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:13,920
some would argue the paperwork is worse; at least the Nazis were straightforward about the killing part).

108
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:23,320
That's also fifty nine-elevens every single day, except nobody invades anyone about it because diseases don't have oil.

109
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:29,360
Your body is quietly falling apart. Your cells are forgetting how to cell properly.

110
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:34,280
Your cancer cells are multiplying RIGHT NOW. Your telomeres are shortening.

111
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:39,380
You are literally dissolving. You're a meat robot with worn-out parts.

112
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:43,100
Every one of these failures is a solvable engineering problem.

113
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:47,020
You'd think humans would prioritize solving these problems.

114
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:52,240
You'd be adorable for thinking that. The Unexplored Therapeutic Frontier.

115
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:58,220
ninety-five percent of your diseases have zero F.D.A.-approved treatments.

116
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:06,100
This means Food and Drug Administration has not administered drugs for ninety-five percent of food-and-drug-related problems.

117
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:10,780
Only fifteen diseases get their first effective treatment each year.

118
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:15,280
six thousand six hundred and fifty diseases are still waiting.

119
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:23,780
There are nine thousand five hundred compounds known safe compounds, and ninety-nine point seven percent of their potential

120
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:31,200
uses have never been tested. At the current discovery rate, finding treatments for all of them will take about four hundred

121
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:36,400
and forty-three years. Everyone currently alive will be dead by then.

122
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:46,780
The Cost of War. Humans spend two point seven two trillion dollars every year on stuff designed specifically to make humans

123
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:55,860
stop being alive: Thirteen thousand nuclear warheads (enough to end civilization thirteen times, just in case the first

124
00:13:55,860 --> 00:14:02,920
twelve apocalypses don't take). A.I. murder-bots. Invisible jets that cost more than hospitals.

125
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:10,080
Space Force (to fight the zero aliens attacking you). And Some kind of earthquake machine (probably).

126
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:16,680
Government spending on clinical trials: six hundred and four times less than military spending.

127
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:21,440
Your chance of dying from terrorism: one in thirty million.

128
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:29,920
Your chance of dying from disease: one hundred percent. If cancer had oil reserves, you would have cured it by two thousand

129
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:38,620
and three. Instead, you spent the repair money on murder tubes that cost more than countries and submarines that hide underwater,

130
00:14:38,940 --> 00:14:43,720
as if that's somehow useful when you live on land. The F.D.A.

131
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:52,960
is Unsafe and Ineffective. Even the money you DO spend on medicine is mostly wasted, because the system that approves treatments

132
00:14:53,240 --> 00:15:00,620
is a smoke detector that works by mail. Vioxx killed an estimated sixty thousand people from heart attacks.

133
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:06,960
The F.D.A. approved it. When patients started dying, someone filled out a P.D.F.

134
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:16,860
form. A P.D.F. Then they faxed it. (Yes, this is how your system works in the twenty-first century.) Then a human read it.

135
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:22,860
Five years and sixty thousand corpses later, someone noticed a pattern.

136
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:31,860
This is your safety system. Your National Institutes of Health, the agency nominally responsible for finding cures, spends

137
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:37,540
three point three percent of its budget on clinical trials (see N.I.H.

138
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:45,240
fails to institute health). The other ninety-six point seven percent goes to basic research, administration, and buildings.

139
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,780
It's like a fire department that spends three percent of its budget on water.

140
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:56,400
Then there's an eight-year delay between proving a drug is safe and letting dying humans take it.

141
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,180
The drug passed the safety test. Everyone agrees it won't kill you.

142
00:16:01,620 --> 00:16:07,560
But you still can't have it because a committee needs to spend eight years making sure it works well enough.

143
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:14,840
You'd volunteer for the trials that would answer that question faster, but so would one point zero eight billion people

144
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:20,500
other patients, and the current system has one point nine zero million patients per year slots.

145
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:24,740
That's a participation rate of zero point zero six percent.

146
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:32,860
It's like a lifeguard who confirms the life preserver floats, then locks it in a cabinet for eight years to study its buoyancy

147
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:38,500
profile while a billion people drown in line for the two available life jackets.

148
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:46,040
Your regulatory system can make two mistakes: approve a bad drug (Type One error), or block a good drug (Type Two error).

149
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:51,300
Your F.D.A. is terrified of the first mistake and completely ignores the second.

150
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:59,680
I calculated the ratio: for every one person protected from a dangerous drug, three thousand and seventy people die waiting

151
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:06,339
for a safe one that's locked in the approval cabinet. Even if you assume a Thalidomide-scale catastrophe happens during

152
00:17:06,339 --> 00:17:13,319
post-phase one efficacy testing every single year (even though it wouldn't because Phase One safety testing actually caught

153
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:20,980
it anyway), the deaths from just the efficacy delay still outnumber the deaths from bad drugs by three thousand and seventy

154
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:25,240
to one. Your safety system's main product is dead patients.

155
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:31,120
The good news: You already know how to fix this. The bad news: It requires you to do something.

156
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:37,020
The weird news: You'll get rich doing it. The Solution. A one percent Treaty.

157
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:45,360
This is going to sound crazy. But you're going to use those papers to persuade the leader of every country on Earth to simultaneously

158
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:49,180
redirect one percent of its military budget to clinical trials.

159
00:17:49,780 --> 00:17:56,820
That's it. That's the treaty. After the craziness objection, the second objection every human has: "But if we cut our military

160
00:17:56,820 --> 00:18:02,440
budget, our enemies will invade us!" Everyone cuts one percent at the same time.

161
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:07,920
If every country reduces by one percent simultaneously, the balance of power doesn't change.

162
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:15,380
Nobody becomes more vulnerable. Nobody gains an advantage. You all just have one percent fewer missiles pointed at you,

163
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:20,200
which you will not notice because you currently have enough to kill everyone twenty times over.

164
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:29,500
Two point six nine trillion dollars is still enough to murder every man, woman, and child on Earth twenty times, which should

165
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:33,700
be more than sufficient. "But humans would never agree to a treaty!"

166
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:40,400
you say. You already have. Multiple times. You banned chemical weapons (nineteen ninety-three, one hundred and ninety-three

167
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:45,780
countries). You banned biological weapons (nineteen seventy-five, one hundred and eighty-seven countries).

168
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:50,380
You banned landmines (nineteen ninety-seven, one hundred and sixty-four countries).

169
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:54,720
You've signed treaties banning weapons you actually like using.

170
00:18:55,360 --> 00:19:01,260
This one just asks you to buy one percent fewer of them. I ran ten thousand simulations of this plan.

171
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:08,220
The math works in every one. The money works in every one. The incentives align in every one.

172
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:15,340
The only variable that produces failure is the percentage of humans who decide it sounds crazy without reading the next

173
00:19:15,340 --> 00:19:23,280
page. That is the same reflex that kept you from inventing antibiotics for two hundred thousand years while bread mold sat

174
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:31,040
right there on your bread. And you have two other advantages, the internet and a new financial instrument designed specifically

175
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:36,420
for harnessing the most powerful force in the universe: human greed.

176
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:41,420
Your D.F.D.A. So what happens with that one percent of military spending?

177
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:49,040
eighty percent of the twenty-seven point two billion dollars goes directly to subsidizing patient participation in pragmatic

178
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:55,340
trials at nine hundred and twenty-nine dollars per patient instead of the usual forty-one thousand dollars.

179
00:19:56,240 --> 00:19:59,560
Patients choose which trials to join; their subsidy follows them.

180
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:06,260
Providers get paid for each participant. No grant committees deciding which diseases are fashionable this year.

181
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:10,300
Pragmatic trials integrate into the standard healthcare system.

182
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:15,340
Real patients participate instead of two hundred people hand-picked by pharmaceutical companies.

183
00:20:16,740 --> 00:20:25,200
The whole thing uses your new D.F.D.A. (a decentralized F.D.A.) protocol that reduces trial costs by forty-four point one

184
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:32,140
times and funds twenty-three point four million patients per year (versus the current one point nine zero million patients

185
00:20:32,140 --> 00:20:37,430
per year). Remember that billion patients drowning in line for two life jackets?

186
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:40,640
Your D.F.D.A. (a decentralized F.D.A.) hands out twenty-three million.

187
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:47,980
This increases the treatment discovery rate twelve point three times, compressing that about four hundred and forty-three

188
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:52,720
years wait to about thirty-six years. Two things save lives.

189
00:20:53,600 --> 00:21:00,320
First, finding cures faster: treatments that would have sat undiscovered for centuries get found two hundred and four years

190
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:08,660
sooner on average. Second, eliminating the eight point two years bureaucratic delay between proving a drug is safe and letting

191
00:21:08,660 --> 00:21:15,780
dying humans take it. Combined, treatments reach patients two hundred and twelve years sooner on average.

192
00:21:16,700 --> 00:21:20,420
That timeline shift prevents ten point seven billion deaths.

193
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:27,060
Real-Time Safety Monitoring. Remember Vioxx and the smoke detector that works by mail?

194
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:31,540
